<title>USA: Nuclear Metals Inc Q4 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Nuclear Metals Inc Q4 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>CONCORD, Mass. 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period ended Sept 30</p>
<p>				1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $1.52   profit	 $0.03</p>
<p> Net loss		   3,633   profit	    65</p>
<p> Sales			5,568		    5,191</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   2,391		    2,385</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $1.27   profit	 $0.22</p>
<p> Net loss		   3,037   profit	   510</p>
<p> Sales		     28,694		   18,784</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   2,389		    2,353</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q4 1996 includes $2.1 million charge for estimated losses on current production contracts at Carolina Metals Inc, a wholly owned subsidiary. Q4 1995 includes a tax benefit of $989,000.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
